KARMA 3.1 – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/eatyourgreensstudio-dotcom/karma-fm1 tag v3.1
(commit 718de454ee8ce0e5c6d12ec5fe5e0ba85d0cb4ba; source: https://github.com/eatyourgreensstudio-dotcom/karma-fm1/archive/718de454ee8ce0e5c6d12ec5fe5e0ba85d0cb4ba.tar.gz).
GPL-3.0-only. KARMA by Ariel Muchnik, a fork of SLOOP (isod89), based on Felucca: Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments;
portions Copyright (C) 2026 Ariel Muchnik, Juan Ignacio Antonucci (Juan Jiant), Kerem Kilic, Charles Vestal, PatttF, Erica Synths and the others its LICENSING.md names.
Ported parts keep their licences (Mutable Instruments' Plaits, Elements, Clouds and stmlib, DaisySP, Rings: MIT; Grids: GPL-3.0-or-later; the LXR-02 drum voices: GPL-3.0-only with Erica Synths' section 7 terms;
the screen reader's announce.c: MPL-2.0; the Terminus screen font is rasterised in: OFL 1.1): KARMA's LICENSING.md and the texts in THIRD_PARTY.txt beside this file.
Not affiliated with or endorsed by Mutable Instruments or Erica Synths. The JieLi SDK files of KARMA's packages are not part of the twin.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/karma_studio.c (GPL-3.0-only, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them in firmware/src/felucca.c's order on KARMA's own host-test base (tests/hostsim.c, as
tests/ui_pages_test.c and web/emu/sloop_web.c do) and links firmware/mi's C++ as tools/plx_host.sh builds it. It replaces only the hardware: keys/LEDs/LCD, ADC (MASTER; battery full),
NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, USB = always configured (SysEx and MIDI out through usb.c's rings), one core (KARMA_DUAL_CORE 0), no USB audio, no TRS MIDI, no serial console,
no USB rescue, no updater (ota.c answers the identity handshake only). Compiled with WASI SDK clang (include shim tools/wasm_shim/sys/wait.h).

Corresponding Source (GNU GPL 3.0, section 6)
The complete corresponding source of this build is https://github.com/eatyourgreensstudio-dotcom/karma-fm1 at commit 718de454ee8ce0e5c6d12ec5fe5e0ba85d0cb4ba
together with FM-1 Companion's build script tools/build_sims.py, the glue tools/studio/karma_studio.c and the shim tools/wasm_shim. A tarball of exactly this commit
(karma-fm1-718de454ee8ce0e5c6d12ec5fe5e0ba85d0cb4ba.tar.gz, made with tools/make_source_tarballs.py) is attached to every
FM-1 Companion release that ships this build: https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/releases
Written offer: for at least three years after the last release that ships this build, the maintainers of
FM-1 Companion will give anyone a copy of that corresponding source on request (https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/issues),
free of charge apart from the cost of physically performing the distribution.
